The array can be sorted by right shifts exactly when it is a rotation of its sorted version. Equivalently, going around the array as a circle, there is at most one position where an element is greater than the next one.

The function counts those "descents" over all adjacent pairs, including the wrap-around pair from the last element back to the first. If the count is at most 1, it returns True. An empty array returns True.

```python
def move_one_ball(arr):
    if not arr:
        return True
    n = len(arr)
    count = 0
    for i in range(n):
        if arr[i] > arr[(i + 1) % n]:
            count += 1
    return count <= 1
```

